((date 2026-11-12) (slug entry-timing-screen)
 (hypothesis
  "Entry-timing screen prompted by the DIS-wein-85 chart walk (record k0 trade 1: E 37.12 = a 1999 high, fill 30 % over the 30-week MA, stopped -14.3 % on the pullback the book calls a second-chance buy). Over every closed trade of record-kseed-2026-10-27 (k0-k4), does (H1) skipping tickets whose screen close is more than X over the MA, (H2) anchoring E at the last-N-week high x 1.005 (what entry_anchor_local_range_weeks does), or (H3) replacing extended screens with a buy-limit at MA x (1+m) for 8 weeks with a book stop, improve realised NAV-% (sum of P&L / NAV at the screen)? Proxy screen: may conclude only build or no-build.")
 (base_scenario
  "entry-timing-screen-2026-11-12: host awk per-trade replay (run.sh) of 2,756 closed trades with store bars over record-kseed-2026-10-27 k0-k4 (top-3000 PIT v12 2000-2026, run tree fc78391dd); replay WMA-30 matches audit ma_value 2,756/2,756; null control (code's own E) reproduces the fill day 92.8 %")
 (window_id top3000-pitv12-2000-2026-record-kseed5-trades) (baseline_label record-kseed-actual)
 (variants
  (((label H1-skip-screen-ext-20) (config_hash entry-screen-h1-skip-ext) (aggregate ()))
   ((label H2-range-top-anchor-n4) (config_hash entry-screen-h2-local-range-anchor) (aggregate ()))
   ((label H3-ma-pullback-x20-m8) (config_hash entry-screen-h3-ma-pullback) (aggregate ()))))
 (verdict Reject)
 (notes
  "NO-BUILD DECISIONS (proxy screen; nothing built for H1 or H3; leans on edge-is-the-fat-tail and the 07-12 entry-shape no-build). H2 is the EXISTING flag entry_anchor_local_range_weeks (default 0). Classification REJECT-as-default / keep-as-axis, as dev/notes/mechanism-flag-inventory-2026-08-09.md lists it (KEEP-AXIS); a screen cannot earn do-not-revive, so this row does not make the flag retirement-eligible. The screen re-derives the flag's real test, dev/experiments/entry-anchor-recovery-2026-10-02/results-2026-10-03.md (investor preset, N = 4/13/26, every value diluted 3/3 salts in both 5-year windows 5d and 5r; no phase 2 and no ledger entry under its rule 8). H1: negative at every X measured at the screen in 5/5 seeds (X=20 %: -53.3/-50.5/-53.7/-60.4/-47.9 NAV-%, 3-4 of 8-10 doubling trades lost); measured at the fill it is negative at X <= 40 % and +0.6..+1.7 at X = 50 % (5/5 seeds, 14-15 trades, next to -28..-38 at 40 %), a knife-edge corner that does not change the verdict; win rate 46 % -> 12.5 % and median trade -1.6 % -> -11.4 % with extension, but the >= 50 % bucket earns the most per trade (+2.16, 10 of 80 doubled; APPS 51.1 %, BBWI 50.8 %); the 30-50 % band (+7..+20) flips to -29..-42 at 30-60 % = knife edge on two names. H2: -57..-121 per seed at N in {2,4,8,13}, k0 N=4 90 % CI [-137.5, -19.0]; 2,188 of 2,688 code E's already sit below the 4-week high (the code buys lower), the anchor demands a new high and 753 never fill. H3 (X=20 %, m=8 %): real -> pullback 53.3->31.6 ... 47.9->36.0; fills beat their control (+40.2 pooled) but 405 of 494 flagged trades never pull back and carry the tail. WHY: all three change WHICH names fill, and the dropped names carry the right tail. The narrow variant that changes the price paid and the position size, not which names fill (cap a stale E), is recorded separately as stale-e-cap-screen. Writeup dev/experiments/entry-timing-screen-2026-11-12/README.md."))
